<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50390" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰλλῠριοί</span></b> , οἱ,
			<u>Illyrians</u>, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			1.196
		</span></i>, etc. (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἱλλ-</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			12.329.24
		</span></i>): <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰλλυρία</span></b> , ἡ, <u>Illyria</u>, <i><span class="en">
			St.Byz.
		</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰλλυρίς</span></b> , ἡ, <i><span class="en">
			Ptol.
			<u>Geog.</u>
			2.16.1
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			App.
			<u>Ill.</u>
			6
		</span></i>; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γονή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					601
				</span></i>
			:—Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰλλυρικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
				<u>Illyrian</u>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κή</span>,
			(sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱστορία</span>), ἡ, title of work by Appian: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κόν,
					τό</span>, the <i>region</i>
			or <i>province of Illyria,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ep.Rom.
				15.19
			</span></i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰλλυρίζω</span></b> ,
				<i>speak the Illyrian language</i>, St. Byz.
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰλλυρία</span>
			:—hence Adv.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰλλυριστί</span></b> , ibid.</div>
